"Collapsed Manifolds With Ricci Bounded Covering Geometry (https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.03774)\nciteturn3academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.2 years ago; We study collapsed manifolds with Ricci bounded covering geometry i.e., Ricci curvature is bounded below and the Riemannian universal cover is non-collapsed or consists of uniform Reifenberg points.\nTitle: Collapsed Manifolds With Ricci Bounded Covering Geometry\nAuthors: Hongzhi Huang, Lingling Kong, Xiaochun Rong, Shicheng Xu\nDate: Sat Aug 11 08:45:08 2018\n\nWe study collapsed manifolds with Ricci bounded covering geometry i.e., Ricci curvature is bounded below and the Riemannian universal cover is non-collapsed or consists of uniform Reifenberg points. Via Ricci flows' techniques, we partially extend the nilpotent structural results of Cheeger-Fukaya-Gromov, on collapsed manifolds with (sectional curvature) local bounded covering geometry, to manifolds with (global) Ricci boundedcovering geometry.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStability of Einstein metrics under Ricci flow (https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.2224)\nciteturn3academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.8 years ago; Title: Stability of Einstein metrics under Ricci flow ... We prove dynamical stability and instability theorems for compact Einstein metrics under the Ricci flow.\nTitle: Stability of Einstein metrics under Ricci flow\nAuthors: Klaus Kroencke\nDate: Sun Dec  8 15:06:18 2013\n\nWe prove dynamical stability and instability theorems for compact Einstein metrics under the Ricci flow. We give a nearly complete charactarization of dynamical stability and instability in terms of the conformal Yamabe invariant and the Laplace spectrum. In particular, we prove dynamical stability of some classes of Einstein manifolds for which it was previously not known. Additionally, we show that the complex projective space with the Fubini-Study metric is surprisingly dynamically unstable.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRicci curvature integrals, local functionals, and the Ricci flow (https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.02449)\nciteturn3academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.1 years ago; Title: Ricci curvature integrals, local functionals, and the Ricci flow\nTitle: Ricci curvature integrals, local functionals, and the Ricci flow\nAuthors: Yuanqing Ma, Bing Wang\nDate: Mon Sep  6 13:25:58 2021\n\nConsider a Riemannian manifold $(M^{m}, g)$ whose volume is the same as the standard sphere $(S^{m}, g_{round})$. If $p>\\frac{m}{2}$ and $\\int_{M} \\left\\{ Rc-(m-1)g\\right\\}_{-}^{p} dv$ is sufficiently small, we show that the normalized Ricci flow initiated from $(M^{m}, g)$ will exist immortally and converge to the standard sphere. The choice of $p$ is optimal.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the structure of almost Einstein manifolds (https://arxiv.org/abs/1202.2912)\nciteturn3academia15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 14.7 years ago; Title: On the structure of almost Einstein manifolds\nTitle: On the structure of almost Einstein manifolds\nAuthors: Gang Tian, Bing Wang\nDate: Tue Feb 14 02:37:11 2012\n\nIn this paper, we study the structure of the limit space of a sequence of almost Einstein manifolds, which are generalizations of Einstein manifolds. Roughly speaking, such manifolds are the initial manifolds of some normalized Ricci flows whose scalar curvatures are almost constants over space-time in the $L^1$-sense, Ricci curvatures are bounded from below at the initial time. Under the non-collapsed condition, we show that the limit space of a sequence of almost Einstein manifolds has most properties which is known for the limit space of Einstein manifolds. As applications, we can apply our structure results to study the properties of K\\\"ahler manifolds.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommunications in Analysis and Geometry (https://archive.intlpress.com/site/pub/files/_fulltext/journals/cag/2020/0028/0002/CAG-2020-0028-0002-a005.pdf)\nciteturn3search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.4 years ago; # Stability of Einstein metrics under Ricci flow**Klaus Kröncke**We prove dynamical stability and instability theorems for compact Einstein metrics under the Ricci flow.\nCommunications in Analysis and Geometry  \nVolume 28, Number 2, 351–394, 2020\n\n# Stability of Einstein metrics under Ricci flow\n\n**Klaus Kröncke**\n\nWe prove dynamical stability and instability theorems for compact Einstein metrics under the Ricci flow. We give a nearly complete characterization of dynamical stability and instability in terms of the conformal Yamabe invariant and the Laplace spectrum. In particular, we prove dynamical stability of some classes of Einstein manifolds for which it was previously not known. Additionally, we show that the complex projective space with the Fubini-Study metric is surprisingly dynamically unstable.\n\n1. **Introduction** .................................................................. 352  \n2. **Notation and conventions** ............................................. 356  \n3. **The expander entropy** .................................................. 357  \n4. **Some technical estimates** ............................................. 361  \n5. **Local maximum of λ and the expander entropy** ............ 367  \n6. **A Lojasiewicz-Simon inequality** .................................... 371  \n7. **Dynamical stability and instability** ................................. 373  \n8. **Einstein metrics with positive scalar curvature** ............. 378  \n9. **Dynamical instability of the complex projective space** .. 382  \nAppendix A. **Variational formulas** ...................................... 389  \n**References** ........................................................................ 391\n\n351--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRi