ion date: 20 July 2015\nPublished in: Journal of the American Mathematical Society (Search for Journal in Brave)\n\nAbstract: In this paper, we study the structure of the limit space of a sequence of almost Einstein manifolds, which are generalizations of Einstein manifolds. Roughly speaking, such manifolds are the initial manifolds of some normalized Ricci flows whose scalar curvatures are almost constants over space-time in the {\\displaystyle {L}^{1}}-sense, Ricci curvatures are bounded from below at the initial time. Under the non-collapsed condition, we show that the limit space of a sequence of almost Einstein manifolds has most properties which is known for the limit space of Einstein manifolds. As applications, we can apply our structure results to study the properties of K\"ahler manifolds.\n\nFull work available at URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/1202.2912\n\n\nzbMATH Keywords\n\nspacetimelimit spacenormalized Ricci flowssequence of almost Einstein manifolds\n\nMathematics Subject Classification ID\n\nGeneral geometric structures on manifolds (almost complex, almost product structures, etc.) (53C15) Special Riemannian manifolds (Einstein, Sasakian, etc.) (53C25) Elliptic equations and elliptic systems (35Jxx) Global differential geometry (53Cxx)--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCollapsed Manifolds With Ricci Bounded Covering Geometry | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/vi/abs/1808.03774)\nciteturn3search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.2 years ago; Crawled: last week; We study collapsed manifolds with Ricci bounded covering geometry i.e., Ricci curvature is bounded below and the Riemannian universal cover is non-collapsed or consists of uniform Reifenberg points.\nSubmitted 11 Aug 2018\n\n# Collapsed Manifolds With Ricci Bounded Covering Geometry\n\nCapital Normal University\n\nHH\n\nHongzhi Huang\n\nLK\n\nLingling Kong\n\nXR\n\nXiaochun Rong\n\nSX\n\nShicheng Xu\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe study collapsed manifolds wit